Nod is MIT-licensed **source code**. The audio under `data/` is not covered by
this licence and is not ours to relicense.

`data/corpus/source/manifest.json` records every seed clip as
"generated by macOS say, not redistributable speech". That is Apple's synthesised
voice output, governed by the macOS software licence agreement, and the MIT grant
below does not extend to it. The derived Track A clips and the
`data/corpus/ladder/` halves are built from that audio and inherit the same
restriction. Track B, a real atypical-speech corpus, is not in this repository at
all. No human recording exists here.

Fork the code freely. The sliced source clips and their manifest *are* committed,
which is what lets `nod_bench.corpus.build` rebuild the derived Track A clips on
a machine without macOS — that is the path `make bench` takes. Regenerating the
seed speech itself needs `say`, so it needs macOS; `nod_bench.seed` does it and
refuses rather than falling back to a tone when `say` is absent. Neither step has
a command-line entry point.

